y Data in the Array
The data defining the list of rays to be traced is placed in an array of  structures of the
following form:
typedef struct
{
double x, y, z, l, m, n, opd, intensity;
double Exr, Exi, Eyr, Eyi, Ezr, Ezi;
int wave, error, vigcode, want_opd;
}DDERAYDATA;
Inside the client program, an array of type DDERAYDATA is created with a declaration such as:
DDERAYDATA MyData[101];
There are four trace modes supported, numbered from 0 to 3, and they correspond to the
actions of GetTrace (mode 0), GetTraceDirect (mode 1), GetPolTrace (mode 2), and
GetPolTraceDirect (mode 3). Each mode requires a slightly different set of data to be placed in
the DDERAYDATA structure. The mode is set by the opd parameter in array position zero.
